 add('For pair weights w and A pair shares s, T=Σw and M=Σw(2s−1). The unbounded tie share shift is **−M/(2T)=(B−A)/(2(A+B))**. A+1 means a **one percentage-point A-minus-B pair margin**, requiring another **0.5 A-share points** in the unbounded solve. A +1 A-share point changes pair margin by +2 points and contributes .02w net votes at fixed weight. All-candidate margin uses T+O instead, so its cushion differs. The saved targets solve Σw[2clip(s+δ,0,1)−1]=gT by bounded bisection; original unbounded shifts remain visible. Negative shifts are valid: every named Democratic pair already won its historical contest. Tie is a benchmark, not a win. [Calculator](data/baselines/calculate.py), [settings](data/baselines/scenario-settings.json), [state scenarios](data/baselines/state-scenarios.csv).')
